Host ABI libraries are copied without modification into the guest payload.
Exact resolved filenames are emitted to build/browser/host-libraries.list.
Their upstream projects/licenses: glibc (LGPL-2.1-or-later), GCC runtime
(GPL-3.0-with-GCC-exception), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), FreeType
(FTL or GPL-2.0), libpng (libpng-2.0), zlib (Zlib), libjpeg-turbo
(IJG/BSD-3-Clause/Zlib), expat (MIT), Brotli (MIT), bzip2 (bzip2-1.0.6).
DejaVu fonts: Bitstream Vera/DejaVu font license, copied alongside fonts.
System CA trust store: copied from /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt.
c-ares: MIT, host development library selected by pkg-config libcares;
the resolved runtime library is included in host-libraries.list.
https://c-ares.org/

RebaneOS surface adapter and build recipes: MIT.
No host browser, proxy, or remote rendering is used. The payload renders
HTML/CSS/images and executes Duktape inside the guest Linux ABI runtime.

